Given:

Marked price = Rs. 2600

Discount = 10% and 30%

**Formula used:**

Successive discount% = {(x + y) - (x × y)/100}

where, x and y are discount 

SP = M.P × {(100 - discount%)/100}

Calculation:

Let x be 10% and y be 30%

Successive discount = {(x + y) - (x × y)/100}

⇒ Successive discount = {(10 + 30) - (10 × 30)/100}

⇒ Successive discount = 40 - 3 = 37%

SP = M.P × {(100 - discount%)/100}

⇒ 2600 × {(100 - 37)/100}

⇒ 2600 × {(63)/100}

⇒ 1638

∴ The selling price of the item is Rs. 1638.

**∴ Option 4 is the correct answer.**
